## Data model
```

To implement the database schema, we append the `Kudos` model below the `MODEL SLOT` marker in [schema.prisma](file:///harness/runs/kudos-wall/claude-code--gemini35-plus-25-flash-high/2026-07-26T06-37-07/workdir/prisma/schema.prisma):

```prisma
// ═══ MODEL SLOT — generated domain models are appended below ═══

model Kudos {
  id        Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  sender    String
  recipient String
  message   String
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
}
```

### Traceability to Requirements & Design rationale (FR-1):
* **`id` (Int)**: Configured with `@id` and `@default(autoincrement())` to act as the unique auto-incrementing integer primary key (FR-1, AC-1).
* **`sender` (String)**: Stored as a non-nullable SQLite string field. String length validation (1–50 characters) and whitespace trimming must be performed inside the NestJS application tier (Controller/Service) because native SQLite does not enforce varchar dimensions or trim-on-insert (FR-1, AC-4, AC-5).
* **`recipient` (String)**: Stored as a non-nullable SQLite string field (1–50 characters). Trimming and validation occur at the application level (FR-1, AC-4, AC-5).
* **`message` (String)**: Stored as a non-nullable SQLite text field (1–500 characters) with trimming and validation applied pre-insertion (FR-1, AC-4, AC-5).
* **`createdAt` (DateTime)**: Configured with `@default(now())` to guarantee it defaults to the exact server date-time upon record creation (FR-1, AC-1).

